course: dictionary
lesson: 9020
title: The skull
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The skull is the hard bony frame of your head. It protects your brain, just as a helmet protects a cyclist's head. «The skull guards the brain and the ribs guard the heart and lungs.»
explain: Skull can also mean a sign. A skull with crossed bones warns of danger or poison, as on old pirate flags. Look at the words around it to find the meaning: «crack turtle shells and caiman skulls» is about animal bones, but a bottle with a skull and crossbones on it means do not touch.
explain: Scientists can learn a lot from a skull. «By looking at a fossil skull, scientists can tell what an animal ate.» The shape of the teeth and the jaw gives the clues, so a skull can show what an animal was like.
fact: The skull is the hard bony frame of the head.
fact: The skull protects the brain, eyes and ears.
fact: «Only one skull bone moves: the lower jaw.»
fact: A skull with crossed bones means danger or poison.
fact: A baby's skull has soft spots that close as the baby grows.
exercise: «The skull guards the brain and the ribs guard the heart and lungs.» What does the skull guard? | The heart | The stomach | *The brain | The lungs
exercise: A bottle has a skull and crossbones on it. What does this sign warn you about? | *Poison, do not touch | A time for lunch | A prize for winning | A good smell
exercise: «Only one skull bone moves: the lower jaw, which swings on a hinge.» According to this sentence, which skull bone moves? | *The lower jaw | The nose | The ears | The top of the head
test: «Helmets protect the skull and brain on bikes and scooters.» Why do cyclists wear helmets? | To carry water | *To protect the skull and brain | To keep warm | To look cool
test: «Their skull is built to soften the blows, and they can hit wood about 20 times a second.» What is the woodpecker's skull built to do? | *Soften the blows | Glow in the dark | Crack shells | Hold food
exam: «A baby's skull has soft spots that close as it grows.» What happens to the soft spots as the baby grows? | *They close | They hurt the baby | They grow hair | They open wider and wider forever
